{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-content-git/src/lib.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T05:04:37.474558Z","id":"387a57ebb09554fb6a907ac1f15cd8c2f92993e20bc7cec47b8f43553f06ab8a","body":{"detail":"write_version commits as the store's committer with message `Version <n>` and only the Clax-Version trailer; GitVersions::publish and the hosted prototype (hosted/src/do/artifact.ts trailers) write Clax-Publisher, Clax-Agent and the publish note. VersionWrite has no place for them, and Store::write_version_then_async learns the version's person inside its transaction (version_authors), after the bytes are written. Fix: give VersionWrite optional version metadata the store fills before the write.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":283},"end":{"line":347},"content_hash":"01bd695e7060b4bf584ddf6226410b4aaaa5540b657c48eb00ad6e7356c460ad"},"summary":"Version commits carry no publisher, agent or note: the ContentStore trait passes none","tags":["status:deferred","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-content-git/src/lib.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T05:04:37.474608Z","id":"311881d58d365f850abc4ee379530c4015e511590c55f377b31db9c1cb11c362","body":{"detail":"main must be at the commit of the newest version below n (compare and swap), so after a git push to main every write_version fails with version_conflict and nothing changes (tests/with_git.rs a_write_after_a_push_to_main_is_refused_and_the_push_kept). That keeps the push, but nothing in core records pushed commits as versions yet (recordPushes in hosted/src/do/artifact.ts; record d5c0c8a4 on crates/clax-git/src/lib.rs). The same holds for a first version while main exists without any version tag.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":283},"end":{"line":347},"content_hash":"01bd695e7060b4bf584ddf6226410b4aaaa5540b657c48eb00ad6e7356c460ad"},"summary":"A write is refused while main holds a commit that is not the predecessor version's (a push), so publishing stays blocked until pushes are recorded as versions","tags":["status:deferred","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-content-git/src/lib.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T05:04:37.474648Z","id":"f5f3fae29fb9c85d8d056198f37970cc2d065f2872a4769e956060cf66e1f0b9","body":{"detail":"remove_version of the only version moves main to its commit's parent, which is none, so the update deletes refs/heads/main. MemoryHost allows it; git's receive-pack refuses deleting the branch HEAD names by default (receive.denyDeleteCurrent), as this crate's own server does, and Cloudflare Artifacts' rule is not known. There the remove fails, changing nothing, and the unrecorded v1 blocks the next write of v1 until removed (content/mod.rs Ordering).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":441},"end":{"line":477},"content_hash":"63260012ff84e9bbc951223f5d7e52428aeb1b5542ed2da3742ff32d98958876"},"summary":"Removing a first version deletes main, which a git remote may refuse as deleting the current branch","tags":["revisit:the Artifacts host is wired and its handling of deleting main is known","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-content-git/src/lib.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T05:04:37.474680Z","id":"304f958d12edd7b6e4fefa6c265531d5e7c7b46c7d487ec8a0d9237351c6e748","body":{"detail":"Only the generic implementation and the in-memory wiring (MemGitContent) exist; the Durable Object stand-in host and the Cloudflare Artifacts host belong in crates/clax-worker. ContentStore::fork has no Store caller either.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":109},"end":{"line":114},"content_hash":"7ae33fc513e8bd23ca4786c51e674f801aba4318e8e5a133dbcc3ad4336a9c59"},"summary":"GitContent is not wired into any Store, daemon or Worker yet","tags":["status:deferred","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-content-git/src/lib.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T05:34:34.818877Z","id":"9a33124b2db0d22fa268f90718df04c549bd8863bf07b225362c7cb179ac1178","body":{"detail":"Only the generic implementation and the in-memory wiring (MemGitContent) exist; the Durable Object stand-in host and the Cloudflare Artifacts host belong in crates/clax-worker. ContentStore::fork has no Store caller either.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":131},"end":{"line":136},"content_hash":"7ae33fc513e8bd23ca4786c51e674f801aba4318e8e5a133dbcc3ad4336a9c59"},"summary":"GitContent is not wired into any Store, daemon or Worker yet","supersedes":"304f958d12edd7b6e4fefa6c265531d5e7c7b46c7d487ec8a0d9237351c6e748","tags":["status:deferred","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-content-git/src/lib.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T05:34:34.834531Z","id":"5fc9c903f53be34fd407d2045e80ecbf2c04bacef81fb971aaf3305f1214448a","body":{"detail":"write_version moves main, compare and swap, from the predecessor's commit or from untagged Clax-Version commits a remove left above it (left_above, lib.rs:305). After a git push to main every write fails with version_conflict and nothing changes (tests/with_git.rs a_write_after_a_push_to_main_is_refused_and_the_push_kept; tests/races.rs a_first_write_is_refused_while_main_holds_a_push_on_a_removed_first_version). That keeps the push, but nothing in core records pushed commits as versions (hosted/src/do/artifact.ts recordPushes; record d5c0c8a4 on crates/clax-git/src/lib.rs). The reconcile that lifts this must, under the artifact's content lock and before a publish's pre-check (and lazily on reads): (1) walk main's first parents back to the commit of v<current_version> (bounded, collapsing beyond the bound to main's head as recordPushes does), skipping commits left_above accepts (untagged, carrying Clax-Version: removed publish attempts, never versions); (2) for each pushed commit, oldest first, create v<n> on it with Repo::apply (create-only, compare and swap; a push may not create it, server.rs is_version_tag) and then record the version row n = current + 1 in one transaction (files from the commit's tree, content types by path, sha256 of each blob, publisher the pushing person, file authors as recordPushes gives them), deleting the tag again when the transaction fails; (3) leave main where it is, so the next write_version finds main at v<n> and proceeds. ContentStore has no method for this yet (one answering main's unrecorded commits with their files, one tagging a commit as version n); FsContent and MemContent would answer none.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":391},"end":{"line":457},"content_hash":"bb1c609c65bdd7e904b889aeaa8d7cd48c455b07ad264b2a00b07396cdf17cff"},"summary":"A write is refused while main holds a commit that is neither the predecessor version's nor one a remove left (a push), so publishing stays blocked until pushes are recorded as versions","supersedes":"311881d58d365f850abc4ee379530c4015e511590c55f377b31db9c1cb11c362","tags":["status:deferred","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-content-git/src/lib.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T05:34:34.836689Z","id":"9326a17d0637bbde76db9741644bf482092c782ed1937bd022a6299d9caaaee3","body":{"detail":"remove_version falls back to deleting the tag alone when the remote refuses the non-fast-forward move of main (git receive.denyNonFastForwards, clax-git's stand-in by default) or for a first version; write_version then builds on such commits (left_above), so git log shows each failed attempt (live-page snapshots roll back routinely when nothing is pending, store/live.rs Store::snapshot_pending) under the version that followed, with its publisher and note. Reads go by tags and never see them. left_above recognises them only by being untagged with a Clax-Version trailer: a pusher who writes that trailer has their push built over by the next write (its tree is not carried, since a write's tree comes from version n - 1), which buries the push rather than refusing the write. Whether Cloudflare Artifacts takes non-fast-forward updates of main from Clax decides how often this happens.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":300},"end":{"line":331},"content_hash":"1fa6e40aa989dba3030b5a364b491d212f0dd14bd63231974f14292cd2c01fef"},"suggested_fix":"Once Artifacts' rules are known: where it refuses force updates, mark the next version's commit (a Clax-Replaces trailer naming the attempts) so log readers and the reconcile can tell attempts from versions without trusting the trailer alone.","summary":"Where a remote refuses moving main back, removed publish attempts stay in main's history as untagged Version commits, and a pushed commit carrying Clax-Version is taken for one","tags":["review","revisit:Cloudflare Artifacts' force-push behaviour is known","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-content-git/src/lib.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T05:34:42.312294Z","id":"74ea0cd87df64586b6510985619764df2f82017265c20fb793dbc5060e3791da","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"9a33124b2db0d22fa268f90718df04c549bd8863bf07b225362c7cb179ac1178","summary":"When ContentStore::fork or ContentStore::copy_version gets a Store caller (hosted forks; re-filing live-page threads, store/site.rs place_copies), it needs a VersionMeta as write_version has (content/mod.rs VersionWrite::meta): today GitContent commits a fork's version 1 and a copy's versions as the store's committer, without Clax-Publisher, where the hosted prototype commits a fork as the forking person.","tags":["session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-content-git/src/lib.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T05:34:53.944252Z","id":"7433e022f59a1ef42f12b12a90fa50fcc430c48c3225877294a2dd0c0e665b1e","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f95e83b3","summary":"VersionWrite carries VersionMeta (person public ID and name, agent name, note), filled by Store::version_meta before the content write; GitContent commits as <name> <<person ID>@users.clax.dev> with the note and Clax-Publisher/Clax-Agent trailers. cargo test -p clax-content-git with_git::git_log_shows_who_published_each_version_and_the_note (git clone + git log --format check) and cargo test -p clax-core a_version_write_names_its_publisher_agent_and_note: ok.","supersedes":"387a57ebb09554fb6a907ac1f15cd8c2f92993e20bc7cec47b8f43553f06ab8a","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-content-git/src/lib.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T05:34:53.946033Z","id":"fd8d9b1afd8aaa33088cb69d0fd6e063e0ff34e77c32e8d8ac4f7d16b40a5b4b","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:fe37ed53","summary":"remove_version never deletes main: a first version's remove deletes its tag alone, and where a remote refuses moving main back the tag goes alone too; the next write builds on the untagged commit. cargo test -p clax-content-git over_http::a_first_version_is_removed_and_written_again_on_a_remote_that_keeps_main and over_http::the_contract_holds_over_receive_pack (receive-pack refusing deleting main and non-fast-forwards): ok.","supersedes":"f5f3fae29fb9c85d8d056198f37970cc2d065f2872a4769e956060cf66e1f0b9","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-content-git/src/lib.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T05:39:04.197129Z","id":"3f536be9f8eff23e680ad75ddbbe5b3b9f254889ddca6f3a2807af5bede60c31","body":{"detail":"GitContent::fork deletes the copied repository when its one ref update fails (lib.rs:545, tests/races.rs a_fork_whose_update_is_refused_leaves_no_repository_and_a_retry_succeeds), ignoring the delete's own error. When that delete fails too, the copy keeps v1..vN copied from the source, so the retry's check of an existing target (lib.rs:482-489) answers present(to, 1) or superseded, naming versions the new artifact never had. It also deletes an existing target repository that has no version tag before forking, which is safe only because a fork's target is a new artifact ID no other writer uses.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":482},"end":{"line":548},"content_hash":"0503b770fc2a5807f347c66a5ae4697340ece9a6093e1defde56ec1f8e8994ca"},"suggested_fix":"Treat a target whose main is the source's copied main (or whose tags all name the source's commits) as a failed copy and delete it before forking again, or return the cleanup failure with the fork's error.","summary":"A fork whose cleanup delete also fails leaves a copy holding the source's version tags, and every retry is refused as version 1 already present","tags":["review","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-content-git/src/lib.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T06:12:27.834848Z","id":"0e8821a34b7f27f26fdc67821877d77e3c7d4fb5da173fa135acfd22f1df67b2","body":{"detail":"Only the generic implementation and the in-memory wiring (MemGitContent) exist; the Durable Object stand-in host and the Cloudflare Artifacts host belong in crates/clax-worker. ContentStore::fork has no Store caller either.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":133},"end":{"line":138},"content_hash":"7ae33fc513e8bd23ca4786c51e674f801aba4318e8e5a133dbcc3ad4336a9c59"},"summary":"GitContent is not wired into any Store, daemon or Worker yet","supersedes":"9a33124b2db0d22fa268f90718df04c549bd8863bf07b225362c7cb179ac1178","tags":["status:deferred","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-content-git/src/lib.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T06:12:27.842378Z","id":"a9734cbe773be6ba4ec7caabe6614476d438b6689c5cfe32b5319afdaaae041b","body":{"detail":"remove_version falls back to deleting the tag alone when the remote refuses the non-fast-forward move of main (git receive.denyNonFastForwards, clax-git's stand-in by default) or for a first version; write_version then builds on such commits (left_above), so git log shows each failed attempt (live-page snapshots roll back routinely when nothing is pending, store/live.rs Store::snapshot_pending) under the version that followed, with its publisher and note. Reads go by tags and never see them. left_above recognises them only by being untagged with a Clax-Version trailer: a pusher who writes that trailer has their push built over by the next write (its tree is not carried, since a write's tree comes from version n - 1), which buries the push rather than refusing the write. Whether Cloudflare Artifacts takes non-fast-forward updates of main from Clax decides how often this happens.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":302},"end":{"line":333},"content_hash":"1fa6e40aa989dba3030b5a364b491d212f0dd14bd63231974f14292cd2c01fef"},"summary":"Where a remote refuses moving main back, removed publish attempts stay in main's history as untagged Version commits, and a pushed commit carrying Clax-Version is taken for one","supersedes":"9326a17d0637bbde76db9741644bf482092c782ed1937bd022a6299d9caaaee3","tags":["review","revisit:Cloudflare Artifacts' force-push behaviour is known","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-content-git/src/lib.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T06:12:27.847533Z","id":"844d6bf0fed4e8093fa2573e5a80a9cf74f2749f8d1186b3888e886e53601e4a","body":{"detail":"write_version moves main, compare and swap, from the predecessor's commit or from untagged Clax-Version commits a remove left above it (left_above, lib.rs:305). After a git push to main every write fails with version_conflict and nothing changes (tests/with_git.rs a_write_after_a_push_to_main_is_refused_and_the_push_kept; tests/races.rs a_first_write_is_refused_while_main_holds_a_push_on_a_removed_first_version). That keeps the push, but nothing in core records pushed commits as versions (hosted/src/do/artifact.ts recordPushes; record d5c0c8a4 on crates/clax-git/src/lib.rs). The reconcile that lifts this must, under the artifact's content lock and before a publish's pre-check (and lazily on reads): (1) walk main's first parents back to the commit of v<current_version> (bounded, collapsing beyond the bound to main's head as recordPushes does), skipping commits left_above accepts (untagged, carrying Clax-Version: removed publish attempts, never versions); (2) for each pushed commit, oldest first, create v<n> on it with Repo::apply (create-only, compare and swap; a push may not create it, server.rs is_version_tag) and then record the version row n = current + 1 in one transaction (files from the commit's tree, content types by path, sha256 of each blob, publisher the pushing person, file authors as recordPushes gives them), deleting the tag again when the transaction fails; (3) leave main where it is, so the next write_version finds main at v<n> and proceeds. ContentStore has no method for this yet (one answering main's unrecorded commits with their files, one tagging a commit as version n); FsContent and MemContent would answer none.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":393},"end":{"line":459},"content_hash":"bb1c609c65bdd7e904b889aeaa8d7cd48c455b07ad264b2a00b07396cdf17cff"},"summary":"A write is refused while main holds a commit that is neither the predecessor version's nor one a remove left (a push), so publishing stays blocked until pushes are recorded as versions","supersedes":"5fc9c903f53be34fd407d2045e80ecbf2c04bacef81fb971aaf3305f1214448a","tags":["status:deferred","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-content-git/src/lib.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T06:12:27.850106Z","id":"b84aff04f5179f23f10db9fb363450d4a900c8a316c903f61e16ba32000faddc","body":{"detail":"GitContent::fork deletes the copied repository when its one ref update fails (lib.rs:545, tests/races.rs a_fork_whose_update_is_refused_leaves_no_repository_and_a_retry_succeeds), ignoring the delete's own error. When that delete fails too, the copy keeps v1..vN copied from the source, so the retry's check of an existing target (lib.rs:482-489) answers present(to, 1) or superseded, naming versions the new artifact never had. It also deletes an existing target repository that has no version tag before forking, which is safe only because a fork's target is a new artifact ID no other writer uses.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":484},"end":{"line":550},"content_hash":"0503b770fc2a5807f347c66a5ae4697340ece9a6093e1defde56ec1f8e8994ca"},"summary":"A fork whose cleanup delete also fails leaves a copy holding the source's version tags, and every retry is refused as version 1 already present","supersedes":"3f536be9f8eff23e680ad75ddbbe5b3b9f254889ddca6f3a2807af5bede60c31","tags":["review","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-content-git/src/lib.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T06:15:48.359070Z","id":"a393ca76583e86175ceb5e2b51e068a809869bb6c732620e156797a83faeef17","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"9a33124b2db0d22fa268f90718df04c549bd8863bf07b225362c7cb179ac1178","summary":"crates/clax-worker/src/repos builds GitContent over the RepoDO stand-in (DoHost) and over Cloudflare Artifacts (ArtifactsHost), with assets in RepoDO, in repos::worker::content_store; the instance Durable Object does not call it yet.","tags":["session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-content-git/src/lib.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T06:38:53.826493Z","id":"aa46b644ccc13507849a8c258df38fd2d99299f76ada9ece323318449a7f6607","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"3f536be9f8eff23e680ad75ddbbe5b3b9f254889ddca6f3a2807af5bede60c31","summary":"On Cloudflare Artifacts the common cause, a copy still FORK_IN_PROGRESS when GitContent opens it, no longer reaches this path: ArtifactsHost::fork (crates/clax-worker/src/repos/artifacts.rs:464-497) waits for the copy and deletes it itself when it does not open in about 9 s (commit f9bc642f). A failure of that delete is still answered, and the leftover still blocks retries as this record describes.","tags":["session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-content-git/src/lib.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T06:38:53.826555Z","id":"a504ff03322f58a54156e61ff5508e4c24a22431a3bc42373415e816b32060b1","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"9a33124b2db0d22fa268f90718df04c549bd8863bf07b225362c7cb179ac1178","summary":"Since commit 1edca34f repos::worker::content_store keeps assets in the ASSETS R2 bucket (crates/clax-worker/src/repos/assets.rs), not in RepoDO, and needs RepoDO only for REPO_STORE=memory","tags":["session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-content-git/src/lib.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T07:42:55.916439Z","id":"df7dfc9b7a8cafa1f825ca00e95b6b4e1e67c999128753e8f635e13721828de9","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"0e8821a34b7f27f26fdc67821877d77e3c7d4fb5da173fa135acfd22f1df67b2","summary":"Since cfe9fdaa the instance Durable Object keeps its content in GitContent (crates/clax-worker/src/instance.rs content_store, repos::worker::content_store, marked needing_executor). node crates/clax-worker/e2e.mjs passes on it, and a clone of a Worker-published artifact from /git/ with a token from /_dev/repos/token shows v1 and v2 tagged, each commit carrying Clax-Version and Clax-Publisher. The daemon does not use it yet. Proposed close for the Worker part.","tags":["session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-content-git/src/lib.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T07:46:07.702691Z","id":"e6a776411ff4d0cffe9f7dbf4ce6de6a53b80e661b60d13ef41314d7f37349df","body":{"detail":"remove_version falls back to deleting the tag alone when the remote refuses the non-fast-forward move of main (git receive.denyNonFastForwards, clax-git's stand-in by default) or for a first version; write_version then builds on such commits (left_above), so git log shows each failed attempt (live-page snapshots roll back routinely when nothing is pending, store/live.rs Store::snapshot_pending) under the version that followed, with its publisher and note. Reads go by tags and never see them. left_above recognises them only by being untagged with a Clax-Version trailer: a pusher who writes that trailer has their push built over by the next write (its tree is not carried, since a write's tree comes from version n - 1), which buries the push rather than refusing the write. Whether Cloudflare Artifacts takes non-fast-forward updates of main from Clax decides how often this happens.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":313},"end":{"line":344},"content_hash":"1fa6e40aa989dba3030b5a364b491d212f0dd14bd63231974f14292cd2c01fef"},"summary":"Where a remote refuses moving main back, removed publish attempts stay in main's history as untagged Version commits, and a pushed commit carrying Clax-Version is taken for one","supersedes":"a9734cbe773be6ba4ec7caabe6614476d438b6689c5cfe32b5319afdaaae041b","tags":["review","revisit:Cloudflare Artifacts' force-push behaviour is known","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-content-git/src/lib.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T07:46:07.706715Z","id":"724f971f823d7a4091732c13e54a55e42b7e1e888816ac2f662eddbff9afc3c9","body":{"detail":"write_version moves main, compare and swap, from the predecessor's commit or from untagged Clax-Version commits a remove left above it (left_above, lib.rs:305). After a git push to main every write fails with version_conflict and nothing changes (tests/with_git.rs a_write_after_a_push_to_main_is_refused_and_the_push_kept; tests/races.rs a_first_write_is_refused_while_main_holds_a_push_on_a_removed_first_version). That keeps the push, but nothing in core records pushed commits as versions (hosted/src/do/artifact.ts recordPushes; record d5c0c8a4 on crates/clax-git/src/lib.rs). The reconcile that lifts this must, under the artifact's content lock and before a publish's pre-check (and lazily on reads): (1) walk main's first parents back to the commit of v<current_version> (bounded, collapsing beyond the bound to main's head as recordPushes does), skipping commits left_above accepts (untagged, carrying Clax-Version: removed publish attempts, never versions); (2) for each pushed commit, oldest first, create v<n> on it with Repo::apply (create-only, compare and swap; a push may not create it, server.rs is_version_tag) and then record the version row n = current + 1 in one transaction (files from the commit's tree, content types by path, sha256 of each blob, publisher the pushing person, file authors as recordPushes gives them), deleting the tag again when the transaction fails; (3) leave main where it is, so the next write_version finds main at v<n> and proceeds. ContentStore has no method for this yet (one answering main's unrecorded commits with their files, one tagging a commit as version n); FsContent and MemContent would answer none.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":408},"end":{"line":474},"content_hash":"bb1c609c65bdd7e904b889aeaa8d7cd48c455b07ad264b2a00b07396cdf17cff"},"summary":"A write is refused while main holds a commit that is neither the predecessor version's nor one a remove left (a push), so publishing stays blocked until pushes are recorded as versions","supersedes":"844d6bf0fed4e8093fa2573e5a80a9cf74f2749f8d1186b3888e886e53601e4a","tags":["status:deferred","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-content-git/src/lib.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T07:46:07.710498Z","id":"2e8ae4e8b08fde135d0c2e17f20afe829db9e4553bd5aa35aa94ca4cd451d4aa","body":{"detail":"GitContent::fork deletes the copied repository when its one ref update fails (lib.rs:545, tests/races.rs a_fork_whose_update_is_refused_leaves_no_repository_and_a_retry_succeeds), ignoring the delete's own error. When that delete fails too, the copy keeps v1..vN copied from the source, so the retry's check of an existing target (lib.rs:482-489) answers present(to, 1) or superseded, naming versions the new artifact never had. It also deletes an existing target repository that has no version tag before forking, which is safe only because a fork's target is a new artifact ID no other writer uses.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":499},"end":{"line":565},"content_hash":"0503b770fc2a5807f347c66a5ae4697340ece9a6093e1defde56ec1f8e8994ca"},"summary":"A fork whose cleanup delete also fails leaves a copy holding the source's version tags, and every retry is refused as version 1 already present","supersedes":"b84aff04f5179f23f10db9fb363450d4a900c8a316c903f61e16ba32000faddc","tags":["review","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-content-git/src/lib.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T09:35:32.220393Z","id":"65727be41317db2cf00276b1e7e25dad8eb93e6776f9117b3afee08424a5a894","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"0e8821a34b7f27f26fdc67821877d77e3c7d4fb5da173fa135acfd22f1df67b2","summary":"ContentStore::fork now has a Store caller and takes the publisher's VersionMeta (fc6a2add): Store::fork_artifact_async (crates/clax-core/src/store/forks.rs) passes the forking person and agent, and GitContent commits v1 as them with Clax-Publisher and Clax-Agent before Clax-Forked-From (tests/store_fork.rs over the memory host, on one connection and the pool; tests/with_git.rs checks git log). copy_version still writes without VersionMeta.","tags":["session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-content-git/src/lib.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T09:48:56.188460Z","id":"bb1750f0be1bd4535454c4a2ebefc0b7cbc3779834f78f5a7a1da2b404c63f66","body":{"detail":"Only the generic implementation and the in-memory wiring (MemGitContent) exist; the Durable Object stand-in host and the Cloudflare Artifacts host belong in crates/clax-worker. ContentStore::fork has no Store caller either.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":134},"end":{"line":139},"content_hash":"7ae33fc513e8bd23ca4786c51e674f801aba4318e8e5a133dbcc3ad4336a9c59"},"summary":"GitContent is not wired into any Store, daemon or Worker yet","supersedes":"0e8821a34b7f27f26fdc67821877d77e3c7d4fb5da173fa135acfd22f1df67b2","tags":["status:deferred","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-content-git/src/lib.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T09:48:56.192257Z","id":"4232d7570784215bd8d16d39a09b180e55368764021547c59e3ced6a94260626","body":{"detail":"remove_version falls back to deleting the tag alone when the remote refuses the non-fast-forward move of main (git receive.denyNonFastForwards, clax-git's stand-in by default) or for a first version; write_version then builds on such commits (left_above), so git log shows each failed attempt (live-page snapshots roll back routinely when nothing is pending, store/live.rs Store::snapshot_pending) under the version that followed, with its publisher and note. Reads go by tags and never see them. left_above recognises them only by being untagged with a Clax-Version trailer: a pusher who writes that trailer has their push built over by the next write (its tree is not carried, since a write's tree comes from version n - 1), which buries the push rather than refusing the write. Whether Cloudflare Artifacts takes non-fast-forward updates of main from Clax decides how often this happens.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":318},"end":{"line":349},"content_hash":"1fa6e40aa989dba3030b5a364b491d212f0dd14bd63231974f14292cd2c01fef"},"summary":"Where a remote refuses moving main back, removed publish attempts stay in main's history as untagged Version commits, and a pushed commit carrying Clax-Version is taken for one","supersedes":"a9734cbe773be6ba4ec7caabe6614476d438b6689c5cfe32b5319afdaaae041b","tags":["review","revisit:Cloudflare Artifacts' force-push behaviour is known","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-content-git/src/lib.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T09:48:56.195749Z","id":"f6fd89c89543e538ecd346de7a76d371ea5f978dda22a59fe14dc0f068012c7d","body":{"detail":"write_version moves main, compare and swap, from the predecessor's commit or from untagged Clax-Version commits a remove left above it (left_above, lib.rs:305). After a git push to main every write fails with version_conflict and nothing changes (tests/with_git.rs a_write_after_a_push_to_main_is_refused_and_the_push_kept; tests/races.rs a_first_write_is_refused_while_main_holds_a_push_on_a_removed_first_version). That keeps the push, but nothing in core records pushed commits as versions (hosted/src/do/artifact.ts recordPushes; record d5c0c8a4 on crates/clax-git/src/lib.rs). The reconcile that lifts this must, under the artifact's content lock and before a publish's pre-check (and lazily on reads): (1) walk main's first parents back to the commit of v<current_version> (bounded, collapsing beyond the bound to main's head as recordPushes does), skipping commits left_above accepts (untagged, carrying Clax-Version: removed publish attempts, never versions); (2) for each pushed commit, oldest first, create v<n> on it with Repo::apply (create-only, compare and swap; a push may not create it, server.rs is_version_tag) and then record the version row n = current + 1 in one transaction (files from the commit's tree, content types by path, sha256 of each blob, publisher the pushing person, file authors as recordPushes gives them), deleting the tag again when the transaction fails; (3) leave main where it is, so the next write_version finds main at v<n> and proceeds. ContentStore has no method for this yet (one answering main's unrecorded commits with their files, one tagging a commit as version n); FsContent and MemContent would answer none.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":409},"end":{"line":475},"content_hash":"bb1c609c65bdd7e904b889aeaa8d7cd48c455b07ad264b2a00b07396cdf17cff"},"summary":"A write is refused while main holds a commit that is neither the predecessor version's nor one a remove left (a push), so publishing stays blocked until pushes are recorded as versions","supersedes":"844d6bf0fed4e8093fa2573e5a80a9cf74f2749f8d1186b3888e886e53601e4a","tags":["status:deferred","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-content-git/src/lib.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T09:48:56.255317Z","id":"263bb1f7a37b865cde30a1037b1e4b54ddc45cc7bccba12e3b206b4509532f77","body":{"detail":"GitContent::fork deletes the copied repository when its one ref update fails (tests/races.rs a_fork_whose_update_is_refused_leaves_no_repository_and_a_retry_succeeds), ignoring the delete's own error. When that delete fails too, the copy keeps v1..vN copied from the source, so the retry's check of an existing target answers present(to, 1) or superseded, naming versions the new artifact never had. It also deletes an existing target repository that has no version tag before forking, which is safe only because a fork's target is a new artifact ID no other writer uses (Store::fork_artifact_async generates it under its content lock).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":477},"end":{"line":566},"content_hash":"e814408965bd0d0fd42c61b8893858db1ea3d228723bc1c02ee95b59bfe725ed"},"summary":"A fork whose cleanup delete also fails leaves a copy holding the source's version tags, and every retry is refused as version 1 already present","supersedes":"b84aff04f5179f23f10db9fb363450d4a900c8a316c903f61e16ba32000faddc","tags":["review","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-content-git/src/lib.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T10:12:08.219911Z","id":"ea3c40312249181550e3a758b8d403bad2da77918d3806e0178c374904520bf0","body":{"detail":"GitContent::fork commits version 1 with parent refs[MAIN] of the copied repository (the source's tip), so forking v1 of a five-version source puts the source's v2..v5 behind the fork's v1, with every file and author they had (tests/store_fork.rs forks_with_history checks versions [3, 2, 1] behind a fork of v2). The hosted prototype does the same and records meta fork_copied_commit (hosted/src/do/artifact.ts initFork) so its historyAuthors check refuses an agent's git token while any author in the repository's history is not visible to it (spec 2026-10-11-clax-dev-hosted-design section 9). Rust serves no git remote yet, so nothing leaks today; once one serves a fork, a reader of the fork who may not read the source, or an agent blind to an author of the source's history, would fetch it.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":526},"end":{"line":556},"content_hash":"63eb3ad63fd6cb61e6d94cab89d356ce80798318626bad74c960e4a3bd9d0035"},"suggested_fix":"Record the copied main commit (or the source's version range) with the fork, and make the git token check of a fork count the source's history's authors, as the prototype's historyAuthors does.","summary":"A git fork's history behind version 1 is the source's main when forked, not the forked version, and nothing records where the fork's own history begins","tags":["forks","git","revisit:a git remote serves artifacts","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-content-git/src/lib.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T10:38:24.027304Z","id":"1af99d27a09a175e4bb58a1aa391f929b74d18e6468339f68f56b703d87006f7","body":{"detail":"GitContent::fork deletes the fork's repository when versions::fork_at or its one ref update fails (tests/races.rs a_fork_whose_update_is_refused_leaves_no_repository_and_a_retry_succeeds), ignoring the delete's own error. When that delete fails too after a pruning host's copy (RepoHost::fork) and before fork_at cuts it back, the copy keeps v1..vN copied from the source, so the retry's check of an existing target answers present(to, 1) or superseded, naming versions the new artifact never had. It also deletes an existing target repository that has no version tag before forking, which is safe only because a fork's target is a new artifact ID no other writer uses (Store::fork_artifact_async generates it under its content lock).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":496},"end":{"line":575},"content_hash":"ca5227876d066ecb93cfc49811d2b7284ef91afdb214f50eed1c4e4cdf1edc20"},"summary":"A fork whose cleanup delete also fails leaves a copy holding the source's version tags, and every retry is refused as version 1 already present","supersedes":"263bb1f7a37b865cde30a1037b1e4b54ddc45cc7bccba12e3b206b4509532f77","tags":["review","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-content-git/src/lib.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T10:38:36.055491Z","id":"194da56fc204cbd590084c7aac3fd4f5e47e551e44e68eb820e24786530f524b","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:d0904589","summary":"Fixed: a fork's repository now ends at the forked version (clax_git::versions::fork_at; v1's parent is the source's v<n> commit; pruning hosts drop what no ref reaches, Artifacts gets a new repository with only what v<n> reaches). cargo test -p clax-content-git a_clone_of_a_fork_holds_nothing_the_source_gained_after_the_forked_version: ok (real git clone of a fork of v2 from a source at v4: git log --all authors Mia, Bo, Ann; no v3/v4 commit, tree or file in rev-list --all --objects; cat-file -e and fetch of each fail; the repository's has_object false). store_fork forks_with_history checks versions [2, 1] behind v1; clax-worker stand_in a_fork_through_the_internal_api_holds_nothing_the_source_gained_after_the_forked_version and artifacts_fake a_fork_through_the_binding_keeps_the_history check the RepoDO held set and the Artifacts fake.","supersedes":"ea3c40312249181550e3a758b8d403bad2da77918d3806e0178c374904520bf0","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-content-git/src/lib.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T10:01:12.026334Z","id":"0fc8a1af399ef0b50a0dd1b285879b8cd4d636c171f113542cecb3a2953a979d","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:c3880b03","summary":"Pushed commits are recorded as versions: GitContent::pushed_commits/pushed_files/tag_pushed/untag_pushed and Store::reconcile_pushes_async (crates/clax-core/src/store/pushes.rs), run before every publish. cargo test -p clax-content-git --test integration pushes: 4 passed (two_pushed_commits_become_versions_published_by_the_pusher, a_path_publish_refuses_is_left_out_of_the_pushed_version_and_named_in_its_note, a_publish_that_did_not_see_a_push_is_a_conflict_and_the_push_a_version, a_store_on_one_connection_records_a_push_before_a_publish). Open points left: d72d8f79, b0be91d0, f6fd74bf.","supersedes":"724f971f823d7a4091732c13e54a55e42b7e1e888816ac2f662eddbff9afc3c9","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-content-git/src/lib.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T10:33:40.304047Z","id":"220644516715c2317a23dafba5623ea0c4d0f7ccf0bec19712fe3a9f44badf6e","body":{"detail":"remove_version falls back to deleting the tag alone when the remote refuses the non-fast-forward move of main (git receive.denyNonFastForwards, clax-git's stand-in by default) or for a first version; write_version then builds on such commits (left_above), so git log shows each failed attempt (live-page snapshots roll back routinely when nothing is pending, store/live.rs Store::snapshot_pending) under the version that followed, with its publisher and note. Reads go by tags and never see them. left_above recognises them only by being untagged with a Clax-Version trailer: a pusher who writes that trailer has their push built over by the next write (its tree is not carried, since a write's tree comes from version n - 1), which buries the push rather than refusing the write. Whether Cloudflare Artifacts takes non-fast-forward updates of main from Clax decides how often this happens.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":356},"end":{"line":387},"content_hash":"1fa6e40aa989dba3030b5a364b491d212f0dd14bd63231974f14292cd2c01fef"},"summary":"Where a remote refuses moving main back, removed publish attempts stay in main's history as untagged Version commits, and a pushed commit carrying Clax-Version is taken for one","supersedes":"e6a776411ff4d0cffe9f7dbf4ce6de6a53b80e661b60d13ef41314d7f37349df","tags":["review","revisit:Cloudflare Artifacts' force-push behaviour is known","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-content-git/src/lib.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T10:33:40.313570Z","id":"b283c8bf4af2365a787ef39fb62982195000610f0212e27a0fe1ed06dd355c7a","body":{"detail":"GitContent::fork deletes the copied repository when its one ref update fails (lib.rs:545, tests/races.rs a_fork_whose_update_is_refused_leaves_no_repository_and_a_retry_succeeds), ignoring the delete's own error. When that delete fails too, the copy keeps v1..vN copied from the source, so the retry's check of an existing target (lib.rs:482-489) answers present(to, 1) or superseded, naming versions the new artifact never had. It also deletes an existing target repository that has no version tag before forking, which is safe only because a fork's target is a new artifact ID no other writer uses.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":542},"end":{"line":608},"content_hash":"0503b770fc2a5807f347c66a5ae4697340ece9a6093e1defde56ec1f8e8994ca"},"summary":"A fork whose cleanup delete also fails leaves a copy holding the source's version tags, and every retry is refused as version 1 already present","supersedes":"2e8ae4e8b08fde135d0c2e17f20afe829db9e4553bd5aa35aa94ca4cd451d4aa","tags":["review","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-content-git/src/lib.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T10:33:40.393820Z","id":"414a2c1c832fb3de855427b8f49b274268882be73f1b0cc88fdf596e4776e13c","body":{"detail":"GitContent::pushed_files reads each changed regular file's blob into memory (Repo::read_object) and Store::record_push only then compares its size with MAX_FILE_BYTES and MAX_BODY_BYTES. The stand-in bounds a push at MAX_WRITE_BYTES (crates/clax-worker/src/repos/db.rs), but a push to Cloudflare Artifacts has no such bound here, so a pushed blob of hundreds of MiB is fetched into the instance object's memory on every reconcile, which runs before every publish of the artifact, and can exhaust it. clax-git's Repo has no call answering an object's size without its content. Fix: give Repo an object-size call (Artifacts' file listing carries sizes) and answer an oversized file as left out without reading it.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":780},"end":{"line":800},"content_hash":"e624d37368d11af1c0dd723b41d5d46052b56f4dc9bc9784a1b7386c21bc7651"},"summary":"pushed_files reads every changed blob whole before the size limits leave it out","tags":["review","revisit:the Worker records pushes to Cloudflare Artifacts","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-content-git/src/lib.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T11:21:53.811508Z","id":"6a8e5ea64ced61eb48a0e00f21d035654cbc9d100651d25ae4ee3518cd2e893d","body":{"detail":"GitContent::fork deletes the fork's repository when versions::fork_at or its one ref update fails (tests/races.rs a_fork_whose_update_is_refused_leaves_no_repository_and_a_retry_succeeds), ignoring the delete's own error. When that delete fails too after a pruning host's copy (RepoHost::fork) and before fork_at cuts it back, the copy keeps v1..vN copied from the source, so the retry's check of an existing target answers present(to, 1) or superseded, naming versions the new artifact never had. It also deletes an existing target repository that has no version tag before forking, which is safe only because a fork's target is a new artifact ID no other writer uses (Store::fork_artifact_async generates it under its content lock).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":539},"end":{"line":618},"content_hash":"ca5227876d066ecb93cfc49811d2b7284ef91afdb214f50eed1c4e4cdf1edc20"},"summary":"A fork whose cleanup delete also fails leaves a copy holding the source's version tags, and every retry is refused as version 1 already present","supersedes":"1af99d27a09a175e4bb58a1aa391f929b74d18e6468339f68f56b703d87006f7","tags":["review","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-content-git/src/lib.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T12:12:33.138878Z","id":"380ea6e987a216ae4f72358b870b505eb5daecef9bab569dcd0016c1e913b18f","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"f6fd89c89543e538ecd346de7a76d371ea5f978dda22a59fe14dc0f068012c7d","summary":"The hosted/ files this record cites were removed in 60298c1d (the TypeScript prototype's retirement); read one at its parent with git show 60298c1d^:hosted/<path>","tags":["session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-content-git/src/lib.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T03:18:07.372891Z","id":"783cbc94ca1f3d83701ad6fc4c50466de97dc85bb14046879224f7c476e9a5c6","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"414a2c1c832fb3de855427b8f49b274268882be73f1b0cc88fdf596e4776e13c","summary":"Since 9565a0ea pushed_files walks within MAX_PUSHED_ENTRIES, reads each blob once and answers files past 16 MiB PushedContent::TooLarge without reading them, so a tree naming one blob at many paths no longer multiplies the reads. A single changed blob is still read whole before its size is known, as this record says.","tags":["session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-content-git/src/lib.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T03:19:46.852512Z","id":"81639c9b0658ac20d1bbb51bca88cfd83ff18fce9e357d99a800b633bed178af","body":{"detail":"GitContent::fork deletes the fork's repository when versions::fork_at or its one ref update fails (tests/races.rs a_fork_whose_update_is_refused_leaves_no_repository_and_a_retry_succeeds), ignoring the delete's own error. When that delete fails too after a pruning host's copy (RepoHost::fork) and before fork_at cuts it back, the copy keeps v1..vN copied from the source, so the retry's check of an existing target answers present(to, 1) or superseded, naming versions the new artifact never had. It also deletes an existing target repository that has no version tag before forking, which is safe only because a fork's target is a new artifact ID no other writer uses (Store::fork_artifact_async generates it under its content lock).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":544},"end":{"line":623},"content_hash":"ca5227876d066ecb93cfc49811d2b7284ef91afdb214f50eed1c4e4cdf1edc20"},"summary":"A fork whose cleanup delete also fails leaves a copy holding the source's version tags, and every retry is refused as version 1 already present","supersedes":"6a8e5ea64ced61eb48a0e00f21d035654cbc9d100651d25ae4ee3518cd2e893d","tags":["review","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-content-git/src/lib.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T12:30:25.931134Z","id":"343cad5f353ef07b27d863aa3f64b2b9d4ef7333019ecf1245743ab589bf7608","body":{"detail":"remove_version falls back to deleting the tag alone when the remote refuses the non-fast-forward move of main (git receive.denyNonFastForwards, clax-git's stand-in by default) or for a first version; write_version then builds on such commits (left_above), so git log shows each failed attempt (live-page snapshots roll back routinely when nothing is pending, store/live.rs Store::snapshot_pending) under the version that followed, with its publisher and note. Reads go by tags and never see them. left_above recognises them only by being untagged with a Clax-Version trailer: a pusher who writes that trailer has their push built over by the next write (its tree is not carried, since a write's tree comes from version n - 1), which buries the push rather than refusing the write. Whether Cloudflare Artifacts takes non-fast-forward updates of main from Clax decides how often this happens.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":381},"end":{"line":412},"content_hash":"1fa6e40aa989dba3030b5a364b491d212f0dd14bd63231974f14292cd2c01fef"},"summary":"Where a remote refuses moving main back, removed publish attempts stay in main's history as untagged Version commits, and a pushed commit carrying Clax-Version is taken for one","supersedes":"220644516715c2317a23dafba5623ea0c4d0f7ccf0bec19712fe3a9f44badf6e","tags":["review","revisit:Cloudflare Artifacts' force-push behaviour is known","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-content-git/src/lib.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T12:31:11.623204Z","id":"7821c5726694751a4ee515fe18c165b503acb9fdcca64e8df9a888c5463e25b4","body":{"kind":"resolve","summary":"Duplicate head left by a merge: the same record as 220644516715c2317a23dafba5623ea0c4d0f7ccf0bec19712fe3a9f44badf6e (kept), re-anchored on a parallel branch.","supersedes":"4232d7570784215bd8d16d39a09b180e55368764021547c59e3ced6a94260626","tags":["reason:duplicate","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-content-git/src/lib.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T12:31:11.629734Z","id":"e0cefc0df93459521f5efbf0c37de657af8ea8a4f987554a73efd9476955c33f","body":{"kind":"resolve","summary":"Duplicate head left by a merge: this is a parallel branch's re-anchor of the record that 0fc8a1af399ef0b50a0dd1b285879b8cd4d636c171f113542cecb3a2953a979d closed (Pushed commits are recorded as versions: GitContent::pushed_commits/pushed_files/tag_pushed/untag_pushed and Store::reconcile_pushes_async (crates/clax-core/src). That close stands in the merged code; this head carries no new content.","supersedes":"f6fd89c89543e538ecd346de7a76d371ea5f978dda22a59fe14dc0f068012c7d","tags":["reason:duplicate","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-content-git/src/lib.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T12:31:11.636437Z","id":"80d6240eafcb01927c992e2de943ea236753c9153e9b7b717017f6dafc3844ce","body":{"kind":"resolve","summary":"Duplicate head left by a merge: the same record as 81639c9b0658ac20d1bbb51bca88cfd83ff18fce9e357d99a800b633bed178af (kept), re-anchored on a parallel branch.","supersedes":"b283c8bf4af2365a787ef39fb62982195000610f0212e27a0fe1ed06dd355c7a","tags":["reason:duplicate","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-content-git/src/lib.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T12:34:33.800076Z","id":"7832393087fb3784c3420a345e726cff3c91f9fac909e940ce2e2cca6c6c3e6d","body":{"detail":"GitContent::pushed_files reads each changed regular file's blob into memory (Repo::read_object) and Store::record_push only then compares its size with MAX_FILE_BYTES and MAX_BODY_BYTES. The stand-in bounds a push at MAX_WRITE_BYTES (crates/clax-worker/src/repos/db.rs), but a push to Cloudflare Artifacts has no such bound here, so a pushed blob of hundreds of MiB is fetched into the instance object's memory on every reconcile, which runs before every publish of the artifact, and can exhaust it. clax-git's Repo has no call answering an object's size without its content. Fix: give Repo an object-size call (Artifacts' file listing carries sizes) and answer an oversized file as left out without reading it.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":804},"end":{"line":837},"content_hash":"b8075847d4c80b84585dc3c1a9575b7947b148e7cf46f116dbf9f1deb80625d5"},"summary":"pushed_files reads every changed blob whole before the size limits leave it out","supersedes":"414a2c1c832fb3de855427b8f49b274268882be73f1b0cc88fdf596e4776e13c","tags":["review","revisit:the Worker records pushes to Cloudflare Artifacts","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-content-git/src/lib.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T12:35:23.233174Z","id":"d961a8a2bae6584ef010f94dbd85d7c7cb30d63d3ba3f430eec178107d8da20e","body":{"kind":"resolve","summary":"No longer true: the Worker's content store is GitContent (crates/clax-worker/src/repos/worker.rs content_store, over RepoDO's stand-in or Cloudflare Artifacts, used by crates/clax-worker/src/instance.rs content_store), and ContentStore::fork has a Store caller (crates/clax-core/src/store/forks.rs:125). The daemon keeps its own content store by design.","supersedes":"bb1750f0be1bd4535454c4a2ebefc0b7cbc3779834f78f5a7a1da2b404c63f66","tags":["reason:obsolete","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-content-git/src/lib.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T12:35:23.268439Z","id":"ea9d66747fa29486885846ddb292f30a3e94aa6c035ca43f2cc0eea1c20ded54","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"7832393087fb3784c3420a345e726cff3c91f9fac909e940ce2e2cca6c6c3e6d","summary":"Changed since recorded: pushed_files now reads each blob once and stops reading once the files answered carry PUSHED_BYTES (16 MiB, crates/clax-content-git/src/lib.rs:210, 805-836). One blob is still read whole before its size is compared, so a single pushed blob of hundreds of MiB is still fetched into memory.","tags":["session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-content-git/src/lib.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T07:34:48.139322Z","id":"1474ea59a0b2633f283d2e8fd580e5d37170703f1d72882ecf7f549c55a7ae55","body":{"detail":"Since 652f225fcffa base_entries keeps only paths in `published`, so a path the base commit holds but the version left out never answers PushedContent::Same: its blob is read again (repo.read_object, whole) on every push that follows, though unchanged. Before, such a path answered Same without a read and record_push skipped it. Three cases now cost a read per push: a file over MAX_FILE_BYTES (16 MB, crates/clax-core/src/publish.rs:9) is read whole into memory and then answered TooLarge; a file at a path check_path refuses or that collides (KeptPaths) is read and counted against PUSHED_BYTES (lib.rs:210) before record_push skips it; a refused icon.svg (up to 16 MB, e.g. too_large) is read and re-judged. In the last two the bytes count toward `total`, so a changed file read after them in tree order can be answered TooLarge and named in the note as over Clax's limits although it fits on its own (e.g. a 12 MB left-out file at a refused path plus a 5 MB changed file). The note's text is unchanged in every case. Related: 78323930 (changed blobs are read whole before the size limits apply).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":783},"end":{"line":797},"content_hash":"a0828d18fc467ec717d4c7d9aeb03a15c121fb09de28005fce111268f5c9b015"},"suggested_fix":"Keep the base commit's whole tree for the comparison and answer a path the version left out whose blob is unchanged with a variant that carries no bytes (e.g. PushedContent::LeftOut), reading again only icon.svg, the one path whose reason record_push recomputes; or take the left-out paths' reasons from the base version's note instead of re-reading. Add a pushes.rs test with a left-out file over MAX_FILE_BYTES and a changed file that fits.","summary":"pushed_files now reads again, on every later push, each regular file the base version left out, so a large left-out file is read whole each push and spends the push's 16 MB read budget","tags":["review","push","perf","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-content-git/src/lib.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T07:34:49.574934Z","id":"09cd5f7848dfee10adbec7aaa498dbc0c49ee27ed40f3c3013edd9ffc9a5dd7f","body":{"detail":"GitContent::pushed_files reads each changed regular file's blob into memory (Repo::read_object) and Store::record_push only then compares its size with MAX_FILE_BYTES and MAX_BODY_BYTES. The stand-in bounds a push at MAX_WRITE_BYTES (crates/clax-worker/src/repos/db.rs), but a push to Cloudflare Artifacts has no such bound here, so a pushed blob of hundreds of MiB is fetched into the instance object's memory on every reconcile, which runs before every publish of the artifact, and can exhaust it. clax-git's Repo has no call answering an object's size without its content. Fix: give Repo an object-size call (Artifacts' file listing carries sizes) and answer an oversized file as left out without reading it.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":807},"end":{"line":840},"content_hash":"b8075847d4c80b84585dc3c1a9575b7947b148e7cf46f116dbf9f1deb80625d5"},"summary":"pushed_files reads every changed blob whole before the size limits leave it out","supersedes":"7832393087fb3784c3420a345e726cff3c91f9fac909e940ce2e2cca6c6c3e6d","tags":["review","revisit:the Worker records pushes to Cloudflare Artifacts","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-content-git/src/lib.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T08:11:57.158403Z","id":"66eede6a465f9f051381167d7d683085695b69e29f864b9828c185c930f082e4","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:652f225fcffa","summary":"Fixed in 652f225fcffa: pushed_files answers a path the base version left out whose blob is unchanged PushedContent::LeftOut, unread and outside PUSHED_BYTES, and record_push names it as left out again; only icon.svg is read again (outside the budget) for the icon rules to name its reason. Tests in crates/clax-content-git/tests/pushes.rs: a_file_a_version_left_out_is_not_read_again_by_a_later_push (a 16 MiB + 1 file answers LeftOut on the next push) and a_file_a_version_left_out_does_not_spend_a_later_pushs_read_bytes (a 12 MiB file at a refused path no longer pushes a 5 MiB changed file past the budget). Both failed before the change (TooLarge; page.txt left out) and pass after: bazel test //crates/clax-content-git:integration //crates/clax-content-git:clax_content_git_lib_test, 2 tests pass. A left-out icon.svg is still read whole each push, as 09cd5f78 describes for changed blobs.","supersedes":"1474ea59a0b2633f283d2e8fd580e5d37170703f1d72882ecf7f549c55a7ae55","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-content-git/src/lib.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T09:19:56.893028Z","id":"e2a01975c1900638962d6528926c6b481239a78e8f47757dcb0108c692a02636","body":{"detail":"The trigger: the hosted Worker is killed after GitContent::write_version moved main and tagged v<n> (one atomic ref update, lib.rs:476-544) and before the step's transaction commits. The Worker shares the router (spec 2026-10-19 §8.1). The resumed step reaches write_version_step_async (crates/clax-store/src/artifacts.rs:1369), which calls record_pushes_locked first because expected > 0. pushed_commits returns the stray commit: this take_while drops only untagged commits, and the stray carries the v<n> tag. record_push then records it as version n with the fallback pusher (Pusher::default()); tag_pushed answers Ok(false) for its own tag (lib.rs:868-870). Version n now exists without the step's document writes and without its step row. The step answers 409 version_moved with current n. A worker that re-plans on version_moved, as spec §18 Review Focus 5 describes, publishes the same change again as n+1: two versions, the first without its documents. FsContent refuses instead (record 94b81ad4). Nothing calls the jobs routes on the Worker yet, so no one hits this before merge.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":724},"end":{"line":747},"content_hash":"6022dcbfdbc6cc8bc6f10e436046023065aa55143e15e7e35cb9efca30a9830a"},"suggested_fix":"Mark each step's version commit with a Clax-Step trailer and have pushed_commits leave such a commit to its step, which replaces it (the fix in the reply to record 94b81ad4).","summary":"On the git store, a killed publish step's unrecorded version is adopted as a push, so the resumed step answers version_moved and a re-plan publishes again","tags":["review","kill-resume","content-store","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-content-git/src/lib.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T11:00:11.737537Z","id":"97a0940324c2fe6a346aa6d52854490cc221a416c48c33c730aedd425ba72dec","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:652f225fcffa","summary":"Fixed: pushed_commits leaves a tagged commit carrying Clax-Step to its step, and GitContent::unrecorded_step reads the trailer, so the resumed step replaces its own stray version instead of meeting it as a push. Test passes: bazelisk test //crates/clax-content-git:integration (steps::a_killed_step_resumes_once_in_git, steps::a_stray_another_step_marked_is_not_replaced_in_git); before the fix the resume answered VersionMoved { current: 2 } and the other step's stray was recorded as version 2.","supersedes":"e2a01975c1900638962d6528926c6b481239a78e8f47757dcb0108c692a02636","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-content-git/src/lib.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T11:08:37.180323Z","id":"76be73f4cac65750840a319f2bbc06f21e0105b7874eba2e75fd6823efbd2ce1","body":{"detail":"write_version moves main to a step's version commit before the row commits, so a clone or fetch in the window after a kill sees it on main. A push on top of it gives pushed_commits the chain [stray (tagged v<n>, Clax-Step), pushed]: take_while drops the stray and answers the pushed commit as version n, whose tag_pushed (artifacts.rs:1520) fails with present(id, n) because v<n> names the stray, so the reconcile only warns (artifacts.rs, 'could not record pushed commits'). The step's resume then finds its own mark and calls remove_version(n), which fails: main is past the commit and the pushed commit carries no Clax-Version, so left_above is false ('version n is left'). Neither the push nor the step can land, and every later publish of the artifact is refused. Before 652f225fcffa the stray was recorded as a push and the pushed commit above it as n+1, and the resume answered version_moved. Fix: skip a tagged Clax-Step commit only when it is main's head (nothing built on it); with commits above it, list it as the push it has become, so the resume answers version_moved as for any moved base. A test in crates/clax-content-git/tests/steps.rs: kill after the content write, push a commit onto main, resume the step and publish again.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":757},"end":{"line":768},"content_hash":"c5223de70545cff9e399b7ccaa4e6b42a3839b8f9632e432ad609c407b5ccdd2"},"summary":"A push built on a step's unrecorded version wedges both the push reconcile and the step's resume","tags":["kill-resume","git","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-content-git/src/lib.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T11:08:37.180429Z","id":"321db3760a040522bfdbc1f0a317444095bc3e74277d87cdcf6d42c2bb930f30","body":{"detail":"Version tags cannot be pushed to the stand-in (crates/clax-git/src/server.rs, VERSION_TAGS), so a forged trailer counts only once the core tags the commit itself: VersionStep::Adopt runs tag_pushed (crates/clax-store/src/artifacts.rs:1520) before the version's transaction. A process killed between the tag and the commit leaves v<n> on a pushed commit whose message carries 'Clax-Step: <anything>'. Before 652f225fcffa the next reconcile adopted it again (tag_pushed answers Ok(false) for the same commit). Now pushed_commits drops it as a step's stray, write_version of n is refused as present, and the artifact takes no publish until the tag is removed by hand. When the forged value equals a live step's mark (clax_store::jobs::step_mark is the job ID and key as JSON, both guessable), that step's resume calls remove_version(n) and moves main back past the pusher's commit. On Cloudflare Artifacts, where pushed tags are not known to be refused (records 14e3dd87, 4c8a2ed1 on crates/clax-git/src/server.rs), a pushed v<n+1> carrying the trailer does the same without the kill. The impact is availability: a collaborator who can push, plus a kill in a narrow window, or a pushable tag. Fix: make the mark unforgeable and decide liveness in the store. Give each step a random nonce, kept in the store and never in content (for example step_mark(id, key, nonce), with the nonce on the job's row or derived by a keyed hash from a home secret). Then (a) record_version_locked replaces n only on an exact match, and (b) the reconcile treats a tagged commit as a step's stray only when its trailer is the mark of an open job's uncommitted step, and otherwise as a push.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":757},"end":{"line":768},"content_hash":"c5223de70545cff9e399b7ccaa4e6b42a3839b8f9632e432ad609c407b5ccdd2"},"summary":"A Clax-Step trailer in a pushed commit's message is trusted as a step's mark once the push reconcile has tagged it","tags":["kill-resume","git","security","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-content-git/src/lib.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T12:13:44.565076Z","id":"9806141214971cdf1b86791b42cfed2d5cc96181a19467909b1c7450219dca35","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:652f225fcffa","summary":"Fixed in 652f225fcffa: a step's mark is [job, key, nonce], the nonce 32 hex characters minted by the store at the step's first write and kept in migration 47's job_step_marks with the artifact and version it writes; jobs::mark_of decides Own, Live, Dead or Foreign, and pushed_commits lists each tagged commit's tag and mark (PushedCommit::marked) for the store to decide. Test steps::a_pushed_commit_forging_a_step_mark_is_a_push (crates/clax-content-git/tests/steps.rs: a pushed, reconcile-tagged commit carrying [\"j1\",\"publish:1\"] or a guessed nonce becomes version 2 as a push, stays on main, and the step answers VersionMoved{current: 2}) fails on the code before it (the pushed commit was removed and replaced by the step) and passes; jobs::tests::only_a_mark_the_store_holds_for_its_version_is_a_steps (652f225fcffa) covers each class. bazelisk test //crates/clax-store:all //crates/clax-content-git:all //crates/clax-server:all //crates/clax-http:all //crates/clax-core:all: all PASSED; //crates/clax-server:integration__1 --test_arg=api_jobs:: --runs_per_test=10: 10 of 10 passed (16 tests each).","supersedes":"321db3760a040522bfdbc1f0a317444095bc3e74277d87cdcf6d42c2bb930f30","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-content-git/src/lib.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T12:13:44.621661Z","id":"7f452008248d5d2ed60fad7367c710487a9f659e26e2ba3d85b558ebd34e3613","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:652f225fcffa","summary":"Fixed in 652f225fcffa: the reconcile leaves a genuinely marked tagged commit to its step only while it is the last pushed commit (main's head), and every content store's unrecorded_step answers a mark only for a version nothing is built on (git: main at the tagged commit). Test steps::a_push_built_on_a_killed_steps_version_records_it_as_a_push (kill after the content write, a commit pushed on top, resume: VersionMoved{current: 3}, versions [1,2,3], a new step on base 3 commits version 4 and a publish makes 5) failed before with 'main ... is not at version 2's commit; version 2 is left' and passes; the content contract checks the built-on case. bazelisk test //crates/clax-store:all //crates/clax-content-git:all //crates/clax-server:all //crates/clax-http:all //crates/clax-core:all: all PASSED; //crates/clax-server:integration__1 --test_arg=api_jobs:: --runs_per_test=10: 10 of 10 passed (16 tests each).","supersedes":"76be73f4cac65750840a319f2bbc06f21e0105b7874eba2e75fd6823efbd2ce1","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-content-git/src/lib.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T12:48:34.779372Z","id":"28cdb563efb296b8a7e09838c617953f9579bddf65b8665cc632242e373a666b","body":{"detail":"unrecorded_step answers a mark only while main is at the tagged commit. On a host that allows a non-fast-forward push (deny_non_fast_forwards false; pushed_commits already handles a main that no longer leads to the current version), main can move from a stray v<n> back to a commit P on v<n-1>. Then the step's resume gets None from unrecorded_step and its write of v<n> is refused as present (the stray's tag is there), and the reconcile's record of P fails in tag_pushed with present for the same tag, every time; a dead step's stray is never removed either, since the Dead branch in crates/clax-store/src/artifacts.rs:1452-1472 also starts from unrecorded_step. Clax's own git server denies non-fast-forward pushes by default (crates/clax-git/src/server.rs:146), so this needs a host configured otherwise. The ContentStore doc (crates/clax-core/src/content/mod.rs, unrecorded_step) says 'has anything built on it', which a moved-off main is not.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":702},"end":{"line":720},"content_hash":"149890035c103842350963ffd87099599fec7734fbd22fcfdfcacd339a969dee"},"suggested_fix":"Answer the mark when main is at the stray or does not reach it (it is not built on), and None only when main's first-parent history passes through it; or have remove_version and the reconcile treat a tagged Clax-Step commit outside main's history as removable by its own or a dead step.","summary":"A stray step version that main moved off without building on it is neither the step's nor a push, and wedges its version number","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-content-git/src/lib.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T15:48:28.880771Z","id":"2ea3e427d4d47767d11b2e9c6d24bc8d2b2939870a5dc5396095a4fe42ad611d","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:652f225fcffa","summary":"unrecorded_step answers the mark unless a version is tagged above it or main's first-parent history passes through it (off_main; a walk longer than MAX_PUSHED + MAX_LEFT answers None); remove_version deletes the tag alone when main is off it; a write clears the stray before reconciling pushes, so the push beside it becomes the version and the write conflicts. Evidence: steps::a_push_beside_a_killed_steps_version_is_recorded_once_the_step_resumes failed before (marked_strays empty) and passes after; bazelisk test //crates/clax-content-git:integration //crates/clax-content-git:clax_content_git_lib_test //crates/clax-store:clax_store_lib_test PASSED.","supersedes":"28cdb563efb296b8a7e09838c617953f9579bddf65b8665cc632242e373a666b","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-content-git/src/lib.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T16:57:07.241224Z","id":"4910ca2cd857908c8743283e411a4ee42c47d0a61eb4bfb39d79db72fc5bf18e","body":{"detail":"remove_version falls back to deleting the tag alone when the remote refuses the non-fast-forward move of main (git receive.denyNonFastForwards, clax-git's stand-in by default) or for a first version; write_version then builds on such commits (left_above), so git log shows each failed attempt (live-page snapshots roll back routinely when nothing is pending, store/live.rs Store::snapshot_pending) under the version that followed, with its publisher and note. Reads go by tags and never see them. left_above recognises them only by being untagged with a Clax-Version trailer: a pusher who writes that trailer has their push built over by the next write (its tree is not carried, since a write's tree comes from version n - 1), which buries the push rather than refusing the write. Whether Cloudflare Artifacts takes non-fast-forward updates of main from Clax decides how often this happens.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":395},"end":{"line":426},"content_hash":"1fa6e40aa989dba3030b5a364b491d212f0dd14bd63231974f14292cd2c01fef"},"summary":"Where a remote refuses moving main back, removed publish attempts stay in main's history as untagged Version commits, and a pushed commit carrying Clax-Version is taken for one","supersedes":"343cad5f353ef07b27d863aa3f64b2b9d4ef7333019ecf1245743ab589bf7608","tags":["review","revisit:Cloudflare Artifacts' force-push behaviour is known","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-content-git/src/lib.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T16:57:07.298827Z","id":"d8af971416cb6ffeb2a5f15c8c61f4e483a7f61eacd97001bb95223e627d61ea","body":{"detail":"GitContent::fork deletes the fork's repository when versions::fork_at or its one ref update fails (tests/races.rs a_fork_whose_update_is_refused_leaves_no_repository_and_a_retry_succeeds), ignoring the delete's own error. When that delete fails too after a pruning host's copy (RepoHost::fork) and before fork_at cuts it back, the copy keeps v1..vN copied from the source, so the retry's check of an existing target answers present(to, 1) or superseded, naming versions the new artifact never had. It also deletes an existing target repository that has no version tag before forking, which is safe only because a fork's target is a new artifact ID no other writer uses (Store::fork_artifact_async generates it under its content lock).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":587},"end":{"line":666},"content_hash":"ca5227876d066ecb93cfc49811d2b7284ef91afdb214f50eed1c4e4cdf1edc20"},"summary":"A fork whose cleanup delete also fails leaves a copy holding the source's version tags, and every retry is refused as version 1 already present","supersedes":"81639c9b0658ac20d1bbb51bca88cfd83ff18fce9e357d99a800b633bed178af","tags":["review","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-content-git/src/lib.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-29T18:31:48.606029Z","id":"8ee7ad46ab8197c163ddc13f35c33c04db7ca6cfbaf86260542112b09d61066c","body":{"detail":"GitContent::pushed_files reads each changed regular file's blob into memory (Repo::read_object) and Store::record_push only then compares its size with MAX_FILE_BYTES and MAX_BODY_BYTES. The stand-in bounds a push at MAX_WRITE_BYTES (crates/clax-worker/src/repos/db.rs), but a push to Cloudflare Artifacts has no such bound here, so a pushed blob of hundreds of MiB is fetched into the instance object's memory on every reconcile, which runs before every publish of the artifact, and can exhaust it. clax-git's Repo has no call answering an object's size without its content. Fix: give Repo an object-size call (Artifacts' file listing carries sizes) and answer an oversized file as left out without reading it.\nRe-anchored unchanged from mailto:alex@kesling.co (session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae)'s record.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":893},"end":{"line":938},"content_hash":"95679a703ec1c288a03d5cfde1a57ec8e08cddb71e5ebd1022febf3017fb2d16"},"summary":"pushed_files reads every changed blob whole before the size limits leave it out","supersedes":"09cd5f7848dfee10adbec7aaa498dbc0c49ee27ed40f3c3013edd9ffc9a5dd7f","tags":["review","revisit:the Worker records pushes to Cloudflare Artifacts","session:claude-code:985c579c-9fcb-4f5b-b70f-deedb4f3ea58"]}}
